  "tagline": "Retired Apache incubator time-series database (ex-CeresDB from Ant Group), written in Rust.",
  "description": "Apache HoraeDB, originally CeresDB from Ant Group, was a cloud-native distributed time-series database written in Rust with a hybrid row/columnar storage engine aimed at both classic metrics and high-cardinality analytical workloads. It entered the Apache Incubator in December 2023 and was rebuilt around object storage for a 2.x line. Community activity faded, and in March 2026 the Incubator retired the podling after a community vote; the GitHub repository is archived and the last release, 2.1.0, dates from November 2024. Existing users should migrate to an actively developed engine such as GreptimeDB, VictoriaMetrics or InfluxDB 3.",
